          "conclusion": "Confirmed TP. The combination of __return_true permission_callback and reliance on a guest-accessible wp_rest nonce for authentication means any user who can fetch a page where OptInMonster is active can submit arbitrary email addresses to the contact list. The fix is to either (a) restrict the permission_callback to is_user_logged_in() or current_user_can('read'), or (b) use a site-specific nonce action that cannot be obtained from the frontend."
        }
      },
